Trust-model paragraph in ARCHITECTURE.md

A 3rd-party reviewer assumed Option A (immutable content) when the
design is Option B: object::update rewrites the content blob, tsk edit
opens $EDITOR on the body, sync propagates edits. Documenting this
forecloses repeat misreads and tells future contributors what stable
id actually promises.

Plan: add a Trust model section to ARCHITECTURE.md stating: stable id
is the SHA of the birth content blob, not an immutability guarantee;
fetched refs are untrusted-but-accepted bytes (same trust grain as
git itself); the server is not a trust boundary; common hosts (GitHub,
Forgejo, Tangled, GitLab) don't support per-refspace permissions, so
